(Bug #110: a quoted one-word name followed by a possessive property in the
 SAME slot - `'nums's length` - already worked before the fix, because the
 placeholder content then contains a space and was routed through the full
 expression parser rather than the broken no-space fast path. This test
 pins that this still works after the fix, alongside the bare-name form on
 the same list, for a type other than the manual's own buffer example.)

a list called 'nums' is [1, 2, 3, 4].
Print "{nums's length}".
Print "{'nums's length}".
